Hello,

Please prepare the 2026 Form 940 for HANGS Construction Services LLC as a dra=
ft for review. We would like to see the year-end FUTA figures now, with the f=
ourth quarter projected, and refresh them in January when the December payrol=
l is final.

Attached are the Q1 2026 year-to-date wages by employee, the Q4 2026 payroll =
projection and the 2026 FUTA deposit log. The Q2 2026 year-to-date wages, the=
 Q3 2026 payroll register and the Q1 and Q2 returns as filed are in the clien=
t folder from the Q3 reports.

The three October payrolls are final. November and December are projected at =
scheduled hours and current pay rates, with no overtime. We plan one hire, a =
laborer for the Weller Street job starting November 16. The December 25 payro=
ll will be paid on December 24.

The Q1 FUTA deposit went through EFTPS on May 1. The payroll system carried t=
he Q2 and Q3 amounts forward because they were under $500.

All of our employees work in Washington. Tomas Arvelo is still paid through a=
ccounts payable for concrete finishing at Tideflats Cold Storage; we plan to =
send him a Form 1099-NEC for 2026.

Dana Whitfield
Controller, HANGS Construction Services LLC
payroll@hangs-gc.example

